  "question": {
    "text": "An aeroplane flying at a constant speed, parallel to the horizontal ground, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>&nbsp;above it is observed at an elevation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math> from a point on the ground. If after five seconds, its elevation from the same point is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math>, then the speed (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>km</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>hr</mi></math>) of the aeroplane is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
